Step 1: Install Required Software
Download & Install XAMPP (for PHP & MySQL)

Download XAMPP

Install it and start Apache & MySQL from the XAMPP Control Panel.

Step 2: Download or Clone the Project
Option 1: Clone from GitHub (Recommended)
Open Git Bash or Command Prompt.

Run the following command:
git clone https://github.com/your-username/SportsPulse.git
Option 2: Download Manually
Download the ZIP file from GitHub.

Extract it and move the folder to:

C:\xampp\htdocs\
Step 3: Set Up the Database
Open phpMyAdmin in your browser by visiting:

http://localhost/phpmyadmin/
Click New and create a database named:

sportspulse_db
Import the sportspulse_db.sql file:

Click Import in phpMyAdmin.

Select sportspulse_db.sql from the project folder.

Click Go to execute.

Step 4: Configure Database Connection
Open the db_connect.php file in the project folder.

Ensure the database credentials match your setup:

$servername = "localhost";
$username = "root";
$password = "";
$dbname = "sportspulse_db";
Step 5: Start the Project
Open XAMPP Control Panel.

Start Apache and MySQL.

Open a browser and visit:

http://localhost/SportsPulse/
